## Freeze and trust boundary

The complete package is finalized only after the final preservation/content/metadata comparisons. pin-names.json lists immutable runtime/support files including itself and package-static-closure.json. package-static-closure.json hashes every selected immutable input except itself; it explicitly excludes execution-release.json, pinned-files.json and package-final-audit.json to avoid recursive hash cycles. The release remains NOT_AUTHORIZED with an exact immutable pin map. pinned-files.json is a redundant map outside that pin set.

package-final-audit.json is the externally supplied final trust anchor: it hashes every other regular file and records the full package pathset and directory metadata, explicitly excluding its own content/metadata. Its own full bytes/SHA-256 are delivered to root outside this package. There is no claim of a self-hash. After freeze, all root/Astra review records must be written outside this package. Preparation is complete for independent whole-package review only; execution remains separately unauthorized.
